WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:01.812
This is the heart of the chapter.

2
00:00:01.812 --> 00:00:06.349
Run against the fakes, Microsoft's
samples show the risk on their own terms.

3
00:00:06.349 --> 00:00:09.650
Graph happily creates a
credential with any subject.

4
00:00:09.650 --> 00:00:13.063
Learn's samples don't even
agree on the GitHub issuer:

5
00:00:13.063 --> 00:00:17.350
one has a trailing slash and the
others don't, and the match is exact.

6
00:00:17.350 --> 00:00:21.128
One template defaults the audience
with a stray leading space,

7
00:00:21.128 --> 00:00:22.363
so it can never match.

8
00:00:22.363 --> 00:00:26.238
And two Learn pages give two
different pull request subjects.

9
00:00:26.238 --> 00:00:30.776
So the code checks each credential against
what the workload will really present,

10
00:00:30.776 --> 00:00:33.770
and derives a subject only
when the format is certain.
